Clear Difference: Standalone VRA vs Script‑Created VRA
The difference is NOT about item, quantity, tax, or script quality.
The difference is HOW NetSuite creates the Vendor Return Authorization internally.

🔹 1. Standalone (UI) Vendor Return Authorization
✅ Why it goes to Pending Return
What you do (Visibly):

Open Purchase Order
Click Create Return Authorization
Save
Click Authorize Return

What NetSuite does (Internally):
✅ Transforms the Purchase Order → Vendor Return Authorization
This transformation:

Keeps PO line IDs
Keeps receipt history
Keeps inventory linkage
Knows which stock must be returned

Result:

NetSuite knows physical inventory must come back
Status after Authorize Return = ✅ Pending Return


🔹 2. Script‑Created Vendor Return Authorization
❌ Why it goes to Pending Credit
What your script does:

Uses record.create()
Sets:

Vendor
Item
Quantity
createdfrom (PO reference)



What NetSuite sees:
❌ A brand‑new transaction
❌ No PO line‑level linkage
❌ No inventory receipt reference

Even if createdfrom = PO, it is only a reference, not a transform.

NetSuite conclusion:

“There is no confirmed physical inventory to return.
This is a financial correction only.”

Result:

Status after Authorize Return = ❌ Pending Credit


🔍 Key Difference in One Line (Most Important)

Setting createdfrom is NOT the same as creating FROM the Purchase Order.


